{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.RogersDilogInflection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.RogersDilogInflection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.rogersL2Bracket_half_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.rogersL2Bracket_half_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/RogersDilogInflection.lean#L63-L68","doc":"**The inflection is forced by the reflection symmetry.** The bracket vanishes at the fixed point\n`z = 1/2` of `z ↦ 1−z` because it is antisymmetric there (`B(1/2) = B(1 − 1/2) = −B(1/2)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.rogersL2_half_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.rogersL2_half_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/RogersDilogInflection.lean#L55-L61","doc":"**The flat trefoil shape `z = 1/2` is an inflection point of the Rogers dilogarithm:**\n`L''(1/2) = 0`.  Hence the single-tetrahedron bar-even (second-order) shape correction vanishes; the\nμ₀ closure's `g₂` (order `h²`) cannot come from the single modulus and must be the octahedral\n`e₂` pairwise term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.rogersL2Bracket_reflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.rogersL2Bracket_reflect","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/RogersDilogInflection.lean#L46-L53","doc":"**Abel-reflection antisymmetry.** The bracket flips sign under `z ↦ 1−z`. This is the structural\nreason for the inflection: `z = 1/2` is the reflection's fixed point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.rogersL2Bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.rogersL2Bracket","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/RogersDilogInflection.lean#L42-L44","doc":"The defining bracket of `rogersL2`, isolated for the antisymmetry statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.rogersL2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.rogersL2","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/RogersDilogInflection.lean#L35-L40","doc":"The **elementary closed form of the Rogers-dilogarithm second derivative**\n`L''(z) = −½·( log z / (1−z)² − log(1−z) / z² )`.  (Only the elementary derivative\n`Li₂'(z) = −log(1−z)/z` is used to obtain this form; no `Li₂` value is needed.)\n-- Ref: [hakimoglu-brown2025] https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10206 (Rogers L-function, eq. 4) ","signatureChunk":0}]}